# Path-level review routing for the security spine.
# Advisory only — branch protection enforcement is a separate settings task
# (see the proposal in issue #43). GitHub still auto-requests these owners
# and shows them on the relevant files/PRs.
#
# The list is derived from the 🔒 markers in docs/agents/module-map.md: every
# path marked there is covered here, and a subsystem marked 🔒 is covered by
# its directory entry rather than by one line per file inside it (which is
# why agent/skills/, github/ and storage/schema/ appear whole). Keep the two
# in sync — a new 🔒 marker without a line here silently drops the review
# routing. A path that does not exist is silently IGNORED by GitHub, so an
# entry left behind by a move routes nothing at all.
#
# The framework half of the spine (agent kernel, RBAC, adapters, router,
# storage, the leaf utils) is no longer in this repo: it ships from
# @swampratnz/agent-base and is reviewed there. Nothing written here can
# route review for a file inside the package.

/.github/                            @swampratnz
/scripts/                            @swampratnz
/src/module/agent/skills/            @swampratnz
/src/module/agent/tools/context.ts   @swampratnz
/src/module/agent/tools/index.ts     @swampratnz
/src/module/agentModule.ts           @swampratnz
/src/module/github/                  @swampratnz
/src/module/storage/schema/          @swampratnz
/tests/security-floor.json           @swampratnz
/docs/SECURITY.md                    @swampratnz
